Ladybird fires no select event when an edit or the value setter moves
the cursor in a text control, and fires one when setSelectionRange(),
select() or setRangeText() changes the selection, collapsed or not.
Blink, WebKit and Gecko do the same. Blink schedules select from
TextControlElement::setSelectionRangeForBinding() when the cached
selection changes; WebKit schedules it from HTMLTextFormControlElement::
setSelectionRange() and setRangeText(), through scheduleSelectEvent();
and Gecko, in SelectionChangeEventDispatcher::OnSelectionChange(), for
selection changes with JS_REASON. Neither editing commands nor the value
setter go through any of those.
